hadiths[85]{hadithnumber,text}:
"567","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, There is no Zakat on less than five camels and also there is no Zakat on less than five Awaq (of silver). (5 Awaq = 22 Fransa Riyals of Yemen or 200 Dirhams.) And there is no Zakat on less than five Awsuq. (A special measure of food-grains"""""
"568","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, There is no Zakat either on a horse or a slave belonging to a Muslim."""""""""""""""""
"569","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) (p.b.u.h) ordered (a person) to collect Zakat, and that person returned and told him that Ibn Jamil, Khalid bin Al-Walid, and `Abbas bin `Abdul Muttalib had refused to give Zakat."""" The Prophet said, """"What made Ibn Jamil refuse to give Zakat though he was a poor man, and was made wealthy by Allah and His Apostle ? But you are unfair in asking Zakat from Khalid as he is keeping his armor for Allah's Cause (for Jihad). As for `Abbas bin `Abdul Muttalib, he is the uncle of Allah's Apostle (p.b.u.h) and Zakat is compulsory on him and he should pay it double."""""""" """"570"""",Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said. While I was sleeping"""""
"570","[AI-translation] The hadith of Ibn ‘Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed the Zakat al-Fitr as a sa‘ of dates or a sa‘ of barley, upon every free person or slave, male or female, among the Muslims."""
"571","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, """"Faith (Belief) consists of more than sixty branches (i.e. parts). And Haya (This term """"Haya"""" covers a large number of concepts which are to be taken together; amongst them are self respect, modesty, bashfulness, and scruple, etc.) is a part of faith."""""""""""""
"572","Narrated Abu Sa`id Al-Khudri:\n\nWe used to give one Sa' of meal or one Sa' of barley or one Sa' of dates, or one Sa' of cottage cheese \nor one Sa' of Raisins (dried grapes) as Zakat-ul-Fitr."""""
"573","Narrated Abu Sa`id Al-Khudri:\n\nIn the lifetime of the Prophet (ﷺ) we used to give one Sa' of food or one Sa' of dates or one Sa' of barley or \none Sa' of Raisins (dried grapes) as Sadaqat-ul-Fitr. And when Muawiya became the Caliph and the \nwheat was (available in abundance) he said, \I think (observe) that one Mudd (of wheat) equals two \nMudds (of any of the above mentioned things)."""""""""""""
"574","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."""" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"""""
"575","Hadith of Abu Dharr: He said, """"I approached him while he was sitting in the shade of the Ka'bah, saying: 'They are the losers, by the Lord of the Ka'bah! They are the losers, by the Lord of the Ka'bah!' I said to myself: 'What is wrong with me? Is there something seen in me? What is wrong with me?' So I sat with him while he was saying it, but I could not remain silent, and there came over me what Allah willed. I said: 'Who are they, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Those with the most wealth, except those who spend thus and thus and thus.'"""""""""""""
"576","Narrated Abu Dhar:\n\nOnce I went to him (the Prophet (ﷺ) ) and he said, \By Allah in Whose Hands my life is (or probably said"""""
"577","While I was walking with the Prophet (ﷺ) at the Hurra of Medina in the evening, the mountain of Uhud appeared before us. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, O Abu Dhar! I would not like to have gold equal to Uhud (mountain) for me"""""
"578","Once I went out at night and found Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) walking all alone accompanied by nobody, and I thought that perhaps he disliked that someone should accompany him. So I walked in the shade, away from the moonlight, but the Prophet (ﷺ) looked behind and saw me and said, Who is that?"""" I replied"""""
"579","The hadith of Abu Dharr from Al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, who said: I sat with a gathering of Quraysh, when a man came with rough hair, clothing, and appearance, until he stood over them and greeted them, then said: """"Give glad tidings to those who hoard wealth of a heated stone that will be heated in the Fire of Hell, then placed on the nipple of one of them until it comes out from the shoulder blade, and placed on the shoulder blade until it comes out from the nipple, trembling."""" Then he turned away and sat by a pillar, and I followed him and sat with him, not knowing who he was. I said to him: """"I do not think the people liked what you said."""" He said: """"They do not understand anything. My close friend told me."""" I said: """"Who is your close friend?"""" He said: """"The Prophet, may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him. O Abu Dharr, do you see Uhud?"""" He said: So I looked at the sun to see how much of the day remained, and I thought that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him, was sending me on an errand for him. I said: """"Yes."""" He said: """"I would not like to have the like of Uhud in gold to spend it all except three dinars. And these people do not understand; they only amass the worldly life. No, by Allah, I will not ask them for worldly things, nor will I ask them for a religious verdict until I meet Allah."""""""""""""
"580","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."""" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"""""
"581","Narrated Jabir:\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) came to know that one of his companions had given the promise of freeing his slave after \nhis death, but as he had no other property than that slave, the Prophet (ﷺ) sold that slave for 800 dirhams \nand sent the price to him."""""
"582","Abu Talha had the largest number of datepalms from amongst the Ansars of Medina. The dearest of his property to him was Bairuha garden which was facing the (Prophet's) Mosque. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) used to enter it and drink of its good fresh water. When the Holy Verse:-- 'By no means shall you attain righteousness unless you spend (in charity) of that which you love.' (3.92) was revealed, Abu Talha got up and said, O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)! Allah says: By no means shall you attain righteousness unless you spend of that which you love"""""
"583","Jabir reported that there happened to pass before Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) an ass the face of which had been cauterised, whereupon he said:Allah has cursed one who has cauterised it (on the face)"""""
"584","Zainab, the wife of `Abdullah said, I was in the Mosque and saw the Prophet (p.b.u.h) saying"""""
"585","Narrated Um Salama:\n\nI said, \O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)! Shall I get a reward (in the Hereafter) if I spend on the children of Abu \nSalama and do not leave them like this and like this (i.e."""""
"586","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, When a Muslim spends something on his family intending to receive Allah's reward it is regarded as Sadaqa for him."""""""""""""""""
"587","Umm 'Atiyya reported:We washed her an odd number of times, i. e. three, five or seven times; and Umm 'Atiyya (further) said: We braided her hair in three plaits"""""
"588","Narrated Aisha:\n\nA man said to the Prophet (p.b.u.h), \My mother died suddenly and I thought that if she had lived she \nwould have given alms. So"""""
"589","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, """"On every Muslim there is enjoined (a compulsory) Sadaqa (alms)."""" They (the people) said, """"If one has nothing?' He said, """"He should work with his hands so that he may benefit himself and give in charity."""" They said, """"If he cannot work or does not work?"""" He said, """"Then he should help the oppressed unhappy person (by word or action or both)."""" They said, """"If he does not do it?"""" He said, """"Then he should enjoin what is good (or said what is reasonable).' They said, """"If he does not do that''' He said, """"Then he should refrain from doing evil, for that will be considered for Him as a Sadaqa (charity) . """""""""""""
"590","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, """"If Allah makes us victorious, our encamping place will be Al-Khaif, the place where the infidels took an oath to be loyal to Heathenism (by boycotting Banu Hashim, the Prophet's folk)."""""
"591","that the Prophet (ﷺ) gave him some sheep to distribute among his companions to slaughter as sacrifices (`Id--al--Adha). A kid goat was left and he told the Prophet (ﷺ) of that whereupon he said to him, Slaughter it as a sacrifice (on your behalf)."""""""""""""
"592","I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, Allah said"""""
"593","Abu Huraira said, The Prophet (ﷺ) said"""""
"594","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, The Hour will not be established till two (huge) groups fight against each other"""""
"595","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, If somebody gives in charity something equal to a date from his honestly earned money ----for nothing ascends to Allah except good---- then Allah will take it in His Right (Hand) and bring it up for its owner as anyone of you brings up a baby horse"""""
"596","""""Save yourself from Hell-fire even by giving half a date-fruit in charity."""""""""""""
"597","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, """"There will be none among you but will be talked to by Allah on the Day of Resurrection, without there being an interpreter between him and Him (Allah) . He will look and see nothing ahead of him, and then he will look (again for the second time) in front of him, and the (Hell) Fire will confront him. So, whoever among you can save himself from the Fire, should do so even with one half of a date (to give in charity)."""""
"598","When we were ordered to give alms, we began to work as porters (to earn something we could give in charity). Abu `Aqil came with one half of a Sa` (special measure for food grains) and another person brought more than he did. So the hypocrites said, Allah is not in need of the alms of this (i.e. Abu `Aqil); and this other person did not give alms but for showing off."""" Then Allah revealed:-- 'Those who criticize such of the Believers who give charity voluntarily and those who could not find to give in charity except what is available to them.' (9.79)"""""""""""""
"599","Abu Huraira said, """"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, 'No one should prevent his neighbor from fixing a wooden peg in his wall."""" Abu Huraira said (to his companions), """"Why do I find you averse to it? By Allah, I certainly will narrate it to you."""""""""""""
"600","Ibn Samura al-'Adawi reported:I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) say, and he then narrated (the above-mentioned hadith)"""""
"601","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."""" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him """"602"""",This hadith has been transmitted by Ibrahim b. Sa'd b. Malik on the authority of his father"""""
"602","[AI-translation] The hadith of Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Muslim, trustworthy treasurer who executes [the distribution], and perhaps he said: who gives what he is commanded to give in full and complete, being content with it, so he delivers it to the one for whom one of the charity-givers has commanded it."""
"603","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, If a woman gives in charity from her house meals without wasting (i.e. being extravagant)"""""
"604","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, """"A woman should not fast (optional fasts) except with her husband's permission if he is at home (staying with her). """"605"""",Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents"""""
"605","[AI-translation] The hadith of Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If a woman spends from her husband's earnings without his permission, then for her is half of his reward."""
"606","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."""" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"""""
"607","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Whoever spends two things in Allah's Cause"""""
"608","I proceeded till I entered upon `Umar (and while I was sitting there), his gate-keeper Yarfa came to him and said,  `Uthman """"609"""",Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents"""""
"609","[AI-translation] The hadith of Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: O women, the Muslim women! Let no neighbor look down upon her neighbor, even for a sheep's hoof."""
"610","Seven will Allah shade in His shade on the Day when there is no shade but His: the just ruler, a youth who grew up in worship of his Lord, a man whose heart is attached to the mosques, two who love each other for Allah, meeting and parting for His sake, a man who is called by a woman of status and beauty but says 'I fear Allah', one who gives charity secretly so his left hand does not know what his right hand spends, and one who remembers Allah in solitude and his eyes overflow with tears. """"611"""",Jabir b. 'Abdullah reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying while the bier of Sa'd b. Mu'adh was placed before them:The Throne of the most Gracious shook at the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh """"612"""",Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said. While I was sleeping"""""
"611","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported: A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, which charity brings the greatest reward?"" He said, ""To give charity while you are healthy and miserly, fearing poverty and hoping for wealth, and do not delay until when it reaches the throat, then you say to so-and-so such and such, and to so-and-so such and so, and it had been for so-and-so..."""""
"612","[AI-translation] Ibn Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said, while he was on the pulpit, and he mentioned charity, abstinence, and begging: ""The upper hand is better than the lower hand; the upper hand is the one that gives, and the lower hand is the one that asks."""""
"613","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, The boy is for the owner of the bed."""""""""""""""""
"614","Narrated Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him): I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then he said, """"O Hakim, this wealth is green and sweet. Whoever takes it with a generous heart is blessed in it, and whoever takes it with an eager soul is not blessed in it, like the one who eats but is not satisfied. The upper hand is better than the lower hand."""" Hakim said, """"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, by Him Who sent you with the truth, I will never ask anyone after you for anything until I depart the world.'"""" Then Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) would invite Hakim to take a gift, but he refused to accept it from him. Then 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) invited him to give him something, but he refused to accept anything from him. 'Umar said, """"O Muslims, I bear witness before you that I offer Hakim his due from this booty, but he refuses to take it."""" So Hakim never asked anyone after the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) until he died."""""
"615","Narrated Muawiya:\n\nI heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, \If Allah wants to do good to a person"""""
"616","A bedouin came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said, My wife has delivered a black child."""" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him"""""
"617","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, """"A man keeps on asking others for something till he comes on the Day of Resurrection without any piece of flesh on his face."""" The Prophet (ﷺ) added, """"On the Day of Resurrection, the Sun will come near (to, the people) to such an extent that the sweat will reach up to the middle of the ears, so, when all the people are in that state, they will ask Adam for help, and then Moses, and then Muhammad (p.b.u.h) ."""" The sub-narrator added """"Muhammad will intercede with Allah to judge amongst the people. He will proceed on till he will hold the ring of the door (of Paradise) and then Allah will exalt him to Maqam Mahmud (the privilege of intercession, etc.). And all the people of the gathering will send their praises to Allah."""""
"618","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, """"If Allah makes us victorious, our encamping place will be Al-Khaif, the place where the infidels took an oath to be loyal to Heathenism (by boycotting Banu Hashim, the Prophet's folk). """"619"""",This hadith has been narrated on the authority of A'mash through a different chain of transmitters"""""
"619","[AI-translation] Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to give me a stipend, and I would say, ""Give it to someone who is poorer than I am."" He would say, ""Take it. If you receive something from this wealth while you are not seeking it nor begging for it, then take it; and whatever you do not seek, do not let your soul follow after it."""""
"620","I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, Nothing is left of the prophetism except Al-Mubashshirat."""" They asked"""""
"621","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, The son of Adam (i.e. man) grows old and so also two (desires) grow old with him"""""
"622","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, """"If Adam's son had a valley full of gold, he would like to have two valleys, for nothing fills his mouth except dust. And Allah forgives him who repents to Him."""""""""""""
"623","I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, While I was sleeping"""""
"624","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Allah created Adam in His picture"""""
"625","Hadith of Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: """"Indeed, what I fear most for you is what Allah brings forth for you of the blessings of the earth."""" It was said: """"And what are the blessings of the earth?"""" He said: """"The adornment of the world."""" A man said to him: """"Does good bring evil?"""" The Prophet (peace be upon him) remained silent until we thought that revelation was being sent down to him. Then he began wiping his forehead and said: """"Where is the questioner?"""" He said: """"I am."""" Abu Sa'id said: """"We praised Allah when that appeared."""" He said: """"Good does not bring anything but good. Indeed, this wealth is sweet vegetation. And everything that the spring rain produces kills by overgrazing or causes illness, except the eater of the khadira. It eats until, when its flanks are distended, it faces the sun, then ruminates, defecates, and urinates, then returns to eat. And indeed, this wealth is sweet. Whoever takes it by its right and puts it in its right, what an excellent aid it is. And whoever takes it by other than its right is like one who eats but is not satisfied."""""""""""""
"626","Ahnaf b. Qais reported:While I was in the company of the (elites) of Quraiah, Abu Dharr came there and he was saying: Give glad tidings to the hoarders of riches that their backs would be branded (so deeply) that (the hot Iron) would come out of their sides, and when the backs of their necks would be branded, it would come out of their foreheads. He (Abu Dharr) then went away and sat down. I asked who he was. They said: He is Abu Dharr. I went to him and said to him: What is this that I heard from you which you were saying before? He said: I said nothing but only that which I heard from their Prophet (ﷺ). I again said: What do you say about this gift? He said: Take it, for today it is a help. But when it becomes a price for your religion, then abandon it"""""
"627","Some Ansdri persons asked fof (something) from Allah's Messenge *-r.+r, -ur- alld he gave them. The again askeC him f(something) and h again gave them. And then they aske him and he gave them again till all that was with him finished. And then h said, If I had anything"""""
"628","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, O Allah! Give food to the family of Muhammad."""""""""""""""""
"629","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\n\nWhile I was walking with the Prophet (ﷺ) who was wearing a Najrani outer garment with a thick hem, a \nbedouin came upon the Prophet (ﷺ) and pulled his garment so violently that I could recognize the impress \nof the hem of the garment on his shoulder, caused by the violence of his pull. Then the bedouin said, \n\Order for me something from Allah's Fortune which you have.\"""" The Prophet (ﷺ) turned to him and \nsmiled"""""
"630","Anas b. Malik is reported as saying:Abu Talha was the one among the Ansar of Medina who possessed the largest property and among his property he valued most was his garden known as Bairaha' which was opposite the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) often visited it and he drank of its sweet water. When this verse was revealed: You will never attain righteousness till you give freely of what you love"""" (iii. 91) """"631"""",This hadith has been narrated on the authority of Hisham with the same chain of transmitters. And in the hadith transmitted by Abu Usama the words are: She did not make any will"""""
"631","[AI-translation] Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) gave a stipend to a group, and I was sitting among them. He left out a man from them whom he had not given, and he was the most beloved to me among them. So I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and spoke privately with him, and I said: ""What is the matter with so-and-so? By Allah, I see him as a believer."" He said: ""Or a Muslim."" I remained silent for a little while; then what I knew about him overcame me, and I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with so-and-so? By Allah, I see him as a believer."" He said: ""Or a Muslim."" I remained silent a little while; then what I knew about him overcame me, and I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with so-and-so? By Allah, I see him as a believer."" He said: ""Or a Muslim."" Then he said: ""Indeed I give to a man, while someone else is more beloved to me than him, fearing that he would be thrown into the Fire on his face."""""
"632","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\n\nWhen Allah favored His Apostle with the properties of Hawazin tribe as Fai (booty), he started giving \nto some Quarries men even up to one-hundred camels each, whereupon some Ansari men said about \nAllah's Messenger (ﷺ), \May Allah forgive His Apostle! He is giving to (men of) Quraish and leaves us"""""
"633","The Prophet (ﷺ) sent for the Ansar (and when they came), he asked, 'Is there any stranger amongst you? They said"""""
"634","On the day of the Conquest of Mecca, when the Prophet (ﷺ) had given (from the booty) the Quraish, the Ansar said, By Allah"""""
"635","When it was the day (of the battle) of Hunain, the tributes of Hawazin and Ghatafan and others, along with their animals and offspring (and wives) came to fight against the Prophet (ﷺ) The Prophet (ﷺ) had with him, ten thousand men and some of the Tulaqa. The companions fled, leaving the Prophet (ﷺ) alone. The Prophet then made two calls which were clearly distinguished from each other. He turned right and said, O the group of Ansar!"""" They said"""""
"636","When Allah gave to His Apostle the war booty on the day of Hunain, he distributed that booty amongst those whose hearts have been (recently) reconciled (to Islam), but did not give anything to the Ansar. So they seemed to have felt angry and sad as they did not get the same as other people had got. The Prophet (ﷺ) then delivered a sermon before them, saying, O"""""
"637","Narrated `Abdullah:\n\nOn the day (of the battle) of Hunain, Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) favored some people in the distribution of the \nbooty (to the exclusion of others); he gave Al-Aqra' bin H`Abis one-hundred camels and he gave \n'Uyaina the same amount, and also gave to some of the eminent Arabs, giving them preference in this \nregard. Then a person came and said, \By Allah"""""
"638","While Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) was distributing the booty at Al-Ja'rana, somebody said to him """"Be just (in your distribution)."""" The Prophet (ﷺ) replied, """"Verily I would be miserable if I did not act justly."""""""""""""
"639","Narrated Abu Sa`id: `Ali sent a piece of gold to the Prophet (ﷺ) who distributed it among four persons: Al-Aqra' bin H`Abis Al-Hanzali from the tribe of Mujashi, 'Uyaina bin Badr Al-Fazari, Zaid at-Ta'i who belonged to (the tribe of) Bani Nahban, and 'Alqama bin Ulatha Al-`Amir who belonged to (the tribe of) Bani Kilab. So the Quraish and the Ansar became angry and said, \He (i.e. the Prophet"""""
"640","`Ali bin Abi Talib sent a piece of gold not yet taken out of its ore, in a tanned leather container to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) . Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) distributed that amongst four Persons: 'Uyaina bin Badr, Aqra bin H`Abis, Zaid Al-Khail and the fourth was either Alqama or Amir bin at-Tufail. On that, one of his companions said, We are more deserving of this (gold) than these (persons)."""" When that news reached the Prophet (ﷺ) """""
"641","I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, While I was sleeping"""""
"642","While we were with Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) a bedouin got up and said, O Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)! Settle my case according to Allah's Book (Laws)."""" Then his opponent got up and said"""""
"643","I relate the traditions of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) to you for I would rather fall from the sky than attribute something to him falsely. But when I tell you a thing which is between you and me, then no doubt, war is guile. I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, In the last days of this world there will appear some young foolish people who will use (in their claim) the best speech of all people (i.e. the Qur'an) and they will abandon Islam as an arrow going through the game. Their belief will not go beyond their throats (i.e. they will have practically no belief)"""""
"644","I asked Sahl bin Hunaif, Did you hear the Prophet (ﷺ) saying anything about Al-Khawarij?"""" He said"""""
"645","Abdullah b. Mas'ud reported that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said:There is none amongst you with whom is not an attache from amongst the jinn (devil). They (the Companions) said: Allah's Messenger, with you too? Thereupon he said: Yes, but Allah helps me against him and so I am safe from his hand and he does not command me but for good """"646"""",Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents"""""
"646","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: ""I return to my family and find a date fallen on my bed; I pick it up to eat it, then I fear that it may be charity, so I throw it away."""""
"647","The Prophet (ﷺ) passed by a fallen date and said, """"Were it not for my doubt that this might have been given in charity, I would have eaten it."""" And narrated Abu Huraira the Prophet (ﷺ) said, """"I found a datefruit fallen on my bed."""""""""""""
"648","Narrated Anas:\n\nSome meat was presented to the Prophet (p.b.u.h) and it had been given to Barira (the freed slave-girl \nof Aisha) in charity. He said, \This meat is a thing of charity for Barira but it is a gift for us.\"""""""""""" """"649"""",Once the Prophet (ﷺ) went to `Aisha and asked her whether she had something (to eat). She said that she had nothing except the mutton which Um 'Atiyya had sent to (Barirah) in charity. The Prophet (ﷺ) said that it had reached its destination (i.e. it is no longer an object of charity.)"""""
"649","[AI-translation] Umm 'Atiyyah al-Ansariyyah said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) entered upon Aisha, and he said, ""Do you have anything?"" She said, ""Nothing except something that Naseebah sent to us from the sheep that you had sent as charity."" He said, ""It has reached its destination."""""
"650","Abdullah b. Mas'ud reported that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said:There is none amongst you with whom is not an attache from amongst the jinn (devil). They (the Companions) said: Allah's Messenger, with you too? Thereupon he said: Yes, but Allah helps me against him and so I am safe from his hand and he does not command me but for good"""""
"651","Asma' reported Allah's Messenger (way peace be upon him) as saying (to her):Spend and do not calculate, (for) Allah would calculate in your case; and do not hoard, otherwise Allah would be withholding from you"""""
